'''''Porella''''' is a large, common, and widespread [[genus]] of [[liverworts]] in [[Order (biology)|order]] [[Porellales]]. It is a member of the [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] [[Porellaceae]] within that order. 

There were 84 species recognized in 2016, most of them from East Asia.<ref>{{cite journal | author=Söderström | year=2016 | title=World checklist of hornworts and liverworts | journal=PhytoKeys | issue=59 | pages=1–826| doi=10.3897/phytokeys.59.6261|display-authors=etal | pmid=26929706 | pmc=4758082 | doi-access=free }}</ref> [[World Flora Online]] accepts 125 species,<ref name="Worldflora">{{cite web |title=''Porella'' L. |url=http://www.worldfloraonline.org/taxon/wfo-4000030935 |website=www.worldfloraonline.org |access-date=3 July 2023}}</ref> and [[GBIF]] accepts 150 species (as of 4 July 2023).<ref name="GBIF"/>

The genus has a wide [[cosmopolitan distribution]] in temperate areas,<ref name="GBIF"/> where it is commonly found growing attached to the bark of trees. Members of the genus have lobed leaves with a large upper lobe and small lower lobe.<ref name=":0">{{Cite journal |last=Barbour |first=Wm. C. |date=1902 |title=Porella |url=https://www.jstor.org/stable/3237914 |journal=The Bryologist |volume=5 |issue=2 |pages=32–36 |doi=10.2307/3237914 |jstor=3237914 |issn=0007-2745|url-access=subscription }}</ref>

Species ''Porella arboris-vitae'', ''Porella bolanderi'',<ref name=":0" /> ''Porella cordeana'', ''Porella navicularis'', ''Porella pinnata'',<ref name=":0" /> ''Porella platyphylla'' and ''Porella roellii'', were all found in Montana, USA.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Ratz |first=David  |title=A Liverwort – Montana Field Guide |url=https://fieldguide.mt.gov/speciesDetail.aspx?elcode=NBHEP2Q0H0 |access-date=15 April 2022 |website=fieldguide.mt.gov |language=en}}</ref>

